  "description": "Broad sweep on OpenWhistle-CNN, after the first sweep showed that augmentation hurts and that all models fail on the same validation windows. Questions, in order: (1) how noisy are the labels? 5-fold cross-validation by recording gives an out-of-fold score to every train window; (2) does leaving out the windows whose out-of-fold score contradicts the label, or training on soft out-of-fold labels, help? (3) how large is the seed-to-seed noise of the validation accuracy? (4) the best model without augmentation; (5) small architectures from keyword spotting and sound event detection (BC-ResNet, CRNN, frequency coordinate); (6) distillation from the best model into small ones; (7) which augmentation hurts, and which regularisation helps (weight decay, generalised cross-entropy, weight averaging, learning rate); (8) cleaning the best model's training data; (9) other widths and backbones. No augmentation unless stated. Every run saves the score of each validation window (best_validation_scores.npy), so label corrections can be applied afterwards to every run. Sized for about 34 h on a laptop GeForce 940MX, ordered so that a sweep stopped early answers the first questions.",
